<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Severians</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 884 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An East Slavic tribe on the Desna, Seym and Sula rivers, whose lands became Chernigov and kept the regional name Siveria.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Severians settled the wooded steppe east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desna-river">Desna</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seym-river">Seym</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sula-river">Sula</a> in the 8th century. Archaeologists connect them with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romny-culture">Romny culture</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hill-fort">hill forts</a>. Like the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polans-eastern">Polans</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vyatichi">Vyatichi</a> they paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazars</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived in fortified settlements on river bluffs and farmed the black earth, trading with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar</a> lands and the Arab world, from which large numbers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coins reached them. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novhorod-siverskyi">Novgorod-Seversky</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyubech">Lyubech</a> grew up in their territory. They faced the steppe directly and bore the brunt of nomad raids.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 884 Oleg forced them to pay tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> instead of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazars</a>. Their land became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a> and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-chernigov">Principality of Chernigov</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-novgorod-seversky">Principality of Novgorod-Seversky</a>. The name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/severia">Siveria</a> survived for the region, and the Severians are last mentioned as a people in the 11th century.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/severians.jpg" alt="Severians" width="320" height="398"><figcaption>Image: SeikoEn · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East_Slavic_tribes_peoples_8th_9th_century.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 884 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Slavic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old East Slavic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Siverians, Severyane</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=742&amp;focus=severians" aria-label="Severians on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5425 431 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Severians lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6131 811h0M5697 681h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5745 687h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5745 687h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Ukraine. <a href="/atlas?year=742&amp;focus=severians">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
